  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_7903221b713c4a7ca32e46f08773942d",
      "statement": "BossHunter browser automation is split between a thin Python facade (browser/__init__.py) and RuntimeClient (browser/client.py) that speak HTTP to a bundled local Node.js CDP proxy (browser/runtime/cdp-proxy.mjs); the proxy attaches to the user's already-logged-in Chrome over CDP, so BossHunter never stores platform credentials.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/browser/__init__.py#L1-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9253445eaf58b54ece065108ac43d4c8b953a627f54c14159c612fccd5cc004e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/browser/client.py#L13-L127",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7f581cd64ef21863f96a94c09a25abcb43891a8b0221f07007cadaeb8094239:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/browser/runtime/cdp-proxy.mjs#L1-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:43b34ca66085b639d9b70a26ee968e25b1fd0214cf3cc7ac6e04d3fe220a5b88:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_950b7c676e4b4ebc9059b239914bb762",
      "statement": "Every facade operation gates on ensure_runtime() and returns a falsy default when the runtime is unavailable; evaluate() specifically returns the falsy RUNTIME_NOT_READY sentinel, which the sender maps to the retryable 'runtime_not_ready' error so infrastructure hiccups are retried separately from the progressive-backoff circuit breaker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/browser/__init__.py#L18-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c701713877b7e59cdb429c85423985743d763586f9fedf0b61332bbaa226331e:"
        },
